# Project rules for Cursor

## Coding style
- Use TypeScript everywhere.
- Prefer React hooks.
- Use Tailwind CSS for styling.

## LLM Agent Rules
- Never modify the backend API contract.
- Always ask before deleting a file.
- Keep components small and composable.

## Prompting instructions
- When generating code, include comments that explain key logic.
- Follow the folder structure example that follows.


your-app/
├─ .cursorrules
├─ .env                # never checked in (local dev)
├─ .env.example        # documented env names (no secrets)
├─ package.json
├─ tsconfig.json
├─ vite.config.ts
├─ public/
│  ├─ index.html
│  └─ prompts/
│     ├─ system.v1.md
│     ├─ tools.json
│     └─ policies.md
├─ src/
│  ├─ app/
│  │  ├─ App.tsx
│  │  └─ routes.tsx
│  ├─ components/
│  │  ├─ blog/
│  │  │  ├─ Blog.tsx
│  │  │  ├─ BlogList.tsx
│  │  │  └─ BlogPost.tsx
│  │  └─ ui/
│  │     ├─ Button.tsx
│  │     └─ Card.tsx
│  ├─ hooks/
│  │  └─ usePrompt.ts
│  ├─ lib/
│  │  ├─ api.ts              # client -> server calls
│  │  ├─ schema.ts           # zod schemas for requests/responses
│  ├─ styles/
│  │  └─ index.css
│  ├─ Pages/
│  │  ├─ Homepage.tsx
│  │  ├─ About.tsx
│  │  └─ etc...
├─ server/                   # server or serverless adapter
│  ├─ index.ts               # Fastify/Express entry (local)
│  └─ routes/
│     └─ agent.ts           # POST /api/agent (calls the LLM)
└─ tests/
   └─ agent.spec.ts
